/-!
# The nonabelian natural closure in 11.5.3

The marked flag supplies the original cardinalities and coranks. Two distinct
field-line residuals generate full SL₃ or Sp₄; generation lifts through the
literal two-core quotient to L. The faithful semilinear action on V₂ gives
the elementary rank bound, and the displacement analysis proves line alignment,
including q=4. E.3.19 then proves K=L₁ implies that W is nonabelian.

`Complete.not_isMulCommutative_of_K_eq` is exported in the `Nonabelian`
namespace as `not_isMulCommutative_of_K_eq`. It retains the genuine preceding
chapter inputs, whose discharge remains with the parent source assembly.
Source: Aschbacher--Smith, 11.5.3, printed pp.779--780.
-/
